#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-upload-pack(1)"
msgstr "git-upload-pack(1)"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr "NAME"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:7
msgid "git-upload-pack - Send objects packed back to git-fetch-pack"
msgstr "git-upload-pack - パックされたオブジェクトをgit-fetch-packに送り返す"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr "SYNOPSIS"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git-upload-pack' [--[no-]strict] [--timeout=<n>] [--stateless-rpc]\n"
"\t\t  [--advertise-refs] <directory>\n"
msgstr ""
"'git-upload-pack' [--[no-]strict] [--timeout=<n>] [--stateless-rpc]\n"
"\t\t  [--advertise-refs] <directory>\n"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "DESCRIPTION"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:19
msgid ""
"Invoked by 'git fetch-pack', learns what objects the other side is missing, "
"and sends them after packing."
msgstr ""
"`git fetch-pack` によって呼び出され、通信の反対側で欠落しているオブジェクトを"
"調べ、パッキング後にそれらを送信します。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:24
msgid ""
"This command is usually not invoked directly by the end user.  The UI for "
"the protocol is on the 'git fetch-pack' side, and the program pair is meant "
"to be used to pull updates from a remote repository.  For push operations, "
"see 'git send-pack'."
msgstr ""
"このコマンドは通常、エンドユーザーによって直接呼び出されることはありません。"
"プロトコルのUIは「git fetch-pack」側にあり、プログラムのペアはリモートリポジ"
"トリから更新をプルするために使用されることを目的としています。プッシュ操作に"
"ついては、「git send-pack」を参照してください。"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr "OPTIONS"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:28
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "`--[no-]strict`"
msgid "--[no-]strict"
msgstr "`--[no-]strict`"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:30
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Do not try <directory>/.git/ if <directory> is no Git directory."
msgid "Do not try <directory>/.git/ if <directory> is not a Git directory."
msgstr "<directory> Gitディレクトリでない場合、 <directory>/.git/ を試さない"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:31
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "`--timeout=<n>`"
msgid "--timeout=<n>"
msgstr "`--timeout=<n>`"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:33
msgid "Interrupt transfer after <n> seconds of inactivity."
msgstr "非アクティブになった <n> 秒後に転送を中断します。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:34
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "`--stateless-rpc`"
msgid "--stateless-rpc"
msgstr "`--stateless-rpc`"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:38
msgid ""
"Perform only a single read-write cycle with stdin and stdout.  This fits "
"with the HTTP POST request processing model where a program may read the "
"request, write a response, and must exit."
msgstr ""
"stdinとstdoutを使用して 読み取り/書き込み サイクルを1回だけ実行します。これ"
"は、プログラムが要求を読み取り、応答を書き込み、終了する必要があるHTTP POST要"
"求処理モデルに適合します。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:39
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "`--http-backend-info-refs`"
msgid "--http-backend-info-refs"
msgstr "`--http-backend-info-refs`"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:46
msgid ""
"Used by linkgit:git-http-backend[1] to serve up `$GIT_URL/info/refs?"
"service=git-upload-pack` requests. See \"Smart Clients\" in linkgit:"
"gitprotocol-http[5] and \"HTTP Transport\" in the linkgit:gitprotocol-v2[5] "
"documentation. Also understood by linkgit:git-receive-pack[1]."
msgstr ""
"`$GIT_URL/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack` リクエストを処理するために "
"linkgit:git-http-backend[1] によって使用されます。 linkgit:gitprotocol-"
"http[5] の「Smart Clients」と linkgit:gitprotocol-v2[5] ドキュメントの「HTTP "
"Transport」を参照してください。 linkgit:git-receive-pack[1] でも理解されま"
"す。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "<directory>"
msgstr "<directory>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:49
msgid "The repository to sync from."
msgstr "同期元のリポジトリ。"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "ENVIRONMENT"
msgstr "ENVIRONMENT"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "`GIT_PROTOCOL`"
msgstr "`GIT_PROTOCOL`"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:57
msgid ""
"Internal variable used for handshaking the wire protocol. Server admins may "
"need to configure some transports to allow this variable to be passed. See "
"the discussion in linkgit:git[1]."
msgstr ""
"ワイヤープロトコルをハンドシェイクするために使用される内部変数。サーバー管理"
"者は、この変数を渡すことができるようにいくつかのトランスポートを構成する必要"
"がある場合があります。 linkgit:git[1] のdiscussionを参照してください。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:67
msgid ""
"When cloning or fetching from a partial repository (i.e., one itself cloned "
"with `--filter`), the server-side `upload-pack` may need to fetch extra "
"objects from its upstream in order to complete the request. By default, "
"`upload-pack` will refuse to perform such a lazy fetch, because `git fetch` "
"may run arbitrary commands specified in configuration and hooks of the "
"source repository (and `upload-pack` tries to be safe to run even in "
"untrusted `.git` directories)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:73
msgid ""
"This is implemented by having `upload-pack` internally set the "
"`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` variable to `1`. If you want to override it (because you "
"are fetching from a partial clone, and you are sure you trust it), you can "
"explicitly set `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` to `0`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "SECURITY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:82
msgid ""
"Most Git commands should not be run in an untrusted `.git` directory (see "
"the section `SECURITY` in linkgit:git[1]). `upload-pack` tries to avoid any "
"dangerous configuration options or hooks from the repository it's serving, "
"making it safe to clone an untrusted directory and run commands on the "
"resulting clone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:86
msgid ""
"For an extra level of safety, you may be able to run `upload-pack` as an "
"alternate user. The details will be platform dependent, but on many systems "
"you can run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-upload-pack.txt:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "    git clone --no-local --upload-pack='sudo -u nobody git-upload-pack' ...\n"
msgstr ""

